Source: aas
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), curl, ca-certificates, pkgconf, libasound2-dev
Standards-Version: 4.5.1
Homepage: https://github.com/hifiberry/aas

Package: aas
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libasound2-plugin-aas (= ${binary:Version}), python3
Description: Alternative audio server
 A small audio server that owns the sound card and mixes the streams of
 its clients. It is an alternative to PipeWire on HiFiBerry OS.
 .
 The package is installed disabled. Nothing changes on a device until
 "hifiberry-audio-server set aas" is run; "hifiberry-audio-server set
 pipewire" switches back. Removing the package switches back too.
 .
 Includes:
  * aas - the audio server
  * aasctl - command-line client for the daemon
  * hifiberry-audio-server - switch between PipeWire and aas
  * aas-config - writes the daemon's configuration at boot

Package: libasound2-plugin-aas
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: ALSA plugin for the aas audio server
 An ALSA PCM and control plugin that plays through the aas daemon and
 sets its volume from ALSA's mixer. Installing it changes nothing until
 the ALSA configuration shipped with the aas package is linked in.
